From db366fffc54732ae39e5b323a5d827121aa13a9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:06:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 74/76] vgpu: run compute kernels that use imageblocks

Component: Vulkan compute reflection.

A compute kernel with an explicit imageblock was refused as an interface
the runtime cannot provision. It is not one: metal2vulkan lowers the
imageblock to a Workgroup array inside the shader and its slice writes
to storage-image writes, so there is nothing for the runtime to bind.
macOS 27's CoreAnimation blurs every Liquid Glass backdrop through such
kernels (backdrop_capture_compute_tile, variable_blur_copy_base_mip,
variable_blur_downsample_compute_agx2), and with them refused the glass
sampled an empty texture and drew flat grey.

This needs metal2vulkan's whole-region slice write (vmapple-cli's
metal2vulkan patch 0004); without it each tile writes one texel.

Measured on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest at protocol 237:
the blur chain's output went from all-zero to 454k non-zero bytes of
256x256 RGBA16F, and the About window drew as frosted glass.

Verified: the reims-vgpu test suite passes; clippy unchanged.
Not verified: the backend-metal and x86 arms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/spirv_bind.rs | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/spirv_bind.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/spirv_bind.rs
index 880bb13fc..3fed9327e 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/spirv_bind.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/spirv_bind.rs
@@ -2300,12 +2300,10 @@ pub fn first_unsupported_vulkan_interface(
             count: 1,
         });
     }
-    if !reflection.imageblock_layouts.is_empty() {
-        return Some(UnsupportedVulkanInterface {
-            feature: "kernel_imageblock",
-            count: reflection.imageblock_layouts.len(),
-        });
-    }
+    // A compute kernel's explicit imageblock is not an interface the runtime
+    // provisions: the translator lowers it to a Workgroup array inside the
+    // shader, and its slice writes to ordinary storage-image writes. macOS 27's
+    // CoreAnimation blurs every Liquid Glass backdrop through such kernels.
     if !reflection.implicit_imageblock_attachments.is_empty() {
         return Some(UnsupportedVulkanInterface {
             feature: "implicit_imageblock_attachments",
-- 
